<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 9 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">Revolutions in Asia</h1><p class="path-tagline">From Meiji Japan to Khomeini's Iran: a century in which Asian peoples overthrew their rulers and remade their states.</p><p class="path-intro">Between 1868 and 1979 revolution remade state after state across Asia. Some revolutions came from above, as when Japan's reformers restored direct imperial rule to modernise the country, or Atatürk rebuilt Turkey as a secular republic; some were risings against colonial rule, in the Philippines, Vietnam and Indonesia; others curbed or overthrew old monarchies, in Persia, China and Iran. This path follows nine of them, from the end of the Tokugawa shogunate to the founding of the Islamic Republic.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Chronicler</a> · <a href="/start">the Strategist</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1868</span><span class="path-step-name">Meiji Restoration</span><span class="path-step-why">The revolution of 1868 that ended the Tokugawa shogunate, restored direct imperial rule and launched Japan's rapid modernisation.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-revolution"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philippine-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1896–1898</span><span class="path-step-name">Philippine Revolution</span><span class="path-step-why">Begun by the Katipunan in 1896 against Spanish rule, it declared independence on 12 June 1898, but Spain then ceded the islands to the United States.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/persian-constitutional-revolution"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/persian-constitutional-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1905–1911</span><span class="path-step-name">Persian Constitutional Revolution</span><span class="path-step-why">Merchants, clergy and reformers forced the Qajar shah to grant a constitution and an elected parliament, the Majlis, in 1906.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xinhai-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1911</span><span class="path-step-name">Xinhai Revolution</span><span class="path-step-why">A mutiny at Wuchang in 1911 spread from province to province until the boy emperor Puyi abdicated and the Republic of China was founded.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/ataturks-reforms"><span class="path-step-ph">5</span><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1923–1938</span><span class="path-step-name">Atatürk's reforms</span><span class="path-step-why">A secular national republic in place of the Ottoman Empire: the caliphate abolished, the Latin alphabet adopted, the vote given to women.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/august-revolution"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/august-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1945</span><span class="path-step-name">August Revolution</span><span class="path-step-why">After Japan's surrender in 1945 the Viet Minh took power across Vietnam, and Ho Chi Minh proclaimed the Democratic Republic on 2 September.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-national-revolution"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indonesian-national-revolution.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1947–1949</span><span class="path-step-name">Indonesian National Revolution</span><span class="path-step-why">Sukarno proclaimed independence in August 1945; after two Dutch offensives, international pressure brought the Netherlands to recognise it in 1949.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chinese-civil-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">8 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1927–1949</span><span class="path-step-name">Chinese Civil War</span><span class="path-step-why">The Communists under Mao Zedong defeated the Nationalists and proclaimed the People's Republic of China in October 1949.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-revolution"><span class="path-step-ph">9</span><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">9 · Encyclopedia · Event · 1978–1979</span><span class="path-step-name">Iranian Revolution</span><span class="path-step-why">Mass protests and strikes drove the shah out of Iran in January 1979, and Khomeini returned to found the Islamic Republic.</span></span></a></li></ol>
